ription":"Per-table row selection, e.g. {ampacity: {material: copper, insulation: pvc, loaded_conductors: 3, method: C}}. A filter that matches nothing is refused with the available values."},"table_select":{"type":"object","description":"Per-table single-row selection, e.g. {derating: {kind: ambient_temperature, insulation: pvc, ambient_c: 40}} or {voltage_drop_limits: {installation_type: A, load_type: other}}."},"power_w":{"type":"number"},"power_kw":{"type":"number"},"voltage_v":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"cos_phi":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":1},"phases":{"type":"integer","enum":[1,3]},"efficiency":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":1},"current_a":{"type":"number"},"length_m":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"section_mm2":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"material":{"type":"string","enum":["copper","aluminium"]},"resistivity_ohm_mm2_per_m":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"reactance_ohm":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"drop_limit_percent":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"derating_product":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"factors":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"allowable_current_a":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"fault_current_a":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"fault_current_ka":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"poles":{"type":"integer"},"trip_curve":{"type":"string"},"transformer":{"type":"object"},"source_impedance_ohm":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"source_short_circuit_mva":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"zero_sequence_impedance_ohm":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0},"loads":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"upstream":{"type":"object"},"downstream":{"type":"object"}},"additionalProperties":False},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":True}},
     {"name":"kompas_cabinet_catalog_search","description":"Search a cabinet equipment catalogue for breakers, RCDs, contactors, relays, terminals, busbars and power supplies by parameters: kind, poles, rating range, trip curve, breaking capacity, leakage current, mount type and overall dimensions. Every returned item carries its source string, and every item with known dimensions also carries a ready-made layout entry (width_mm, height_mm, rail_offset_mm) so a pick can go straight into kompas_cabinet_layout_build or into kompas_cabinet_calc. No catalogue data is built in: the catalogue is supplied in the catalog field or loaded from catalog_path inside the project root. The bundled data/cabinet_catalog.example.json is a placeholder of typical DIN 43880 modular dimensions with no manufacturers or article numbers, and any answer built on it is flagged example=True. Items missing required dimensions go to unverified instead of being filled with a typical value. Pure search, no COM, no KOMPAS.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"catalog":{"description":"Catalogue inline: list of rows or {items, source, example}."},"catalog_path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to a JSON catalogue inside the project root."},"query":{"type":"object","description":"Filters: kind, poles, rating_min_a, rating_max_a, trip_curve, breaking_ka_min, leakage_ma, rcd_type, mount, width_max_mm, height_max_mm, depth_max_mm, manufacturer, series, text."},"kind":{"type":"string"},"poles":{},"rating_min_a":{"type":"number"},"rating_max_a":{"type":"number"},"trip_curve":{"type":"string"},"breaking_ka_min":{"type":"number"},"leakage_ma":{"type":"number"},"rcd_type":{"type":"string"},"mount":{"type":"string"},"width_max_mm":{"type":"number"},"height_max_mm":{"type":"number"},"text":{"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"need_geometry":{"type":"boolean","description":"Move items without dimensions to unverified."}},"additionalProperties":False},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":True}},
+    {"name":"kompas_cabinet_spec","description":"Turn a cabinet layout into documents: kind=bom builds the parts list from the layout (what stands, how many, which overall size, at which coordinates); kind=marking assigns positional designations by GOST 2.710-81 letter codes (QF1, KM1, XT1) numbered in the order the items read on the plate - top to bottom, then left to right; kind=labels produces nameplates with the designation, optional item name and the coordinates to place them on. Letter codes come from the caller as codes={lib_key: QF}, or from the item kind via kinds={lib_key: breaker} resolved through the bundled designation_map table, whose source is echoed in provenance. The mapping item kind to letter code is compiled, not quoted: GOST 2.710-81 assigns codes to kinds of element in a diagram, not to kinds of cabinet product, and no code exists there for an RCD - such a position goes to unresolved rather than borrowing the breaker code. Positions absent from the library keep no invented name. Writing the list into a KOMPAS document is not done here: this returns data. Pure, no COM, no KOMPAS.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","required":["kind"],"properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["bom","marking","labels"]},"layout":{"type":"object","description":"Layout produced by kompas_cabinet_layout_build: plate, library, elements, groups, ducts."},"plate":{"type":"object"},"library":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"elements":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"groups":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"ducts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}},"codes":{"type":"object","description":"Explicit letter codes: {lib_key: QF}. Highest priority."},"kinds":{"type":"object","description":"Item kinds: {lib_key: breaker|contactor|terminal|rcd|fuse|relay|disconnect_switch|busbar|psu|surge_protector}. Resolved through designation_map."},"tables":{"type":"object","description":"Override tables, e.g. {designation_map: normative:designation_map} or inline rows."},"with_name":{"type":"boolean","description":"Append the item name to the nameplate text."}},"additionalProperties":False},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":True}},
     {"name":"kompas_docs_search","description":"Full-text search over the project documentation and normative documents on disk, returning a citation for every hit: file, line number and the fragment itself. Every answer is traceable to a real file, so it can be verified instead of trusted. Search is substring-based, not semantic: all query words must appear on the line, so an imprecise query returns nothing rather than a plausible answer. Reading is limited to the project root and the current directory; a path outside them is refused. Scanning stops at max_files and reports truncated, so an empty result under truncation does not mean the subject is absent. Binary and unreadable files are skipped. No network access and no COM.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","required":["query"],"properties":{"query":{"description":"Search string, or a list of strings; all words must match."},"root":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to scan; defaults to the project root."},"extensions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"context_lines":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"max_results":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"max_files":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"case_sensitive":{"type":"boolean"}},"additionalProperties":False},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":True}},
     {"name":"kompas_normative_tables","description":"Normative tables as data. The repository now ships the tables the calculation engine needs, each with document, table number, URL, publisher and retrieval date. kind=list inventories what is present and what is missing and why. kind=get returns rows, optionally filtered by field values. kind=validate checks a caller-supplied table against the schema before it is used in a calculation. Sources: GOST R 50571.5.52-2011 (IEC 60364-5-52) cable ampacity, correction factors for ambient temperature and grouping, and voltage-drop limits; GOST R 50345-2010 (IEC 60898-1) time-current trip bands for curves B, C and D; PUE 7th edition clause 6.3.39 for the one demand factor it norms; IEK published product cards for the breaker catalogue. Filtering is not optional convenience: the ampacity table holds every installation method, and selecting across all of them at once would return the smallest section permitted by the most favourable method, which is plausible and wrong. A filter that matches no row is refused together with the list of available values. The demand factor table is partial on purpose - PUE has no demand-factor table, so uncovered load types are reported as unverified instead of being filled with a typical coefficient. Data only, no calculation, no COM.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["list","get","validate"],"description":"list inventories the registry, get returns rows, validate checks rows against the schema."},"table":{"type":"string","enum":["ampacity","breakers","trip_curves","derating","voltage_drop_limits","demand_factors"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Alias for table."},"filter":{"type":"object","description":"Row selection by field values, e.g. {material: copper, insulation: pvc, loaded_conductors: 3, method: C}."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Return at most this many rows; truncated is reported."},"rows":{"type":"array","d